    "chunk_size_bytes": 1694,
    "chunk_text": "Kandy trader fined for hiding 28 Litro gas cylinders\n\nColombo, Nov. 2 (Daily Mirror) - A trader in Kandy has been fined by the Kandy Magistrate\u2019s Court for claiming that gas cylinders were unavailable while keeping 28 Litro LPG cylinders in stock.\n\nThe Court also ordered the confiscation of all 28 cylinders, each weighing 12.5kg, which were seized during a raid conducted by the Consumer Affairs Authority (CAA).\n\nLegal action was taken against D.D. Gurusinghe Trading, an authorised Litro Gas sales outlet at No. 124, Kotugodella Street, Kandy.\n\nThe special raid was carried out by investigation officers of the CAA\u2019s Kandy District Office on October 29, following complaints from consumers.\n\nDuring the operation, a CAA officer posing as a customer visited the outlet and requested a 12.5kg Litro gas cylinder. However, the trader claimed that no cylinders were available for sale.\n\nFollowing the refusal, CAA officers inspected the premises and found 28 Litro gas cylinders despite the trader\u2019s claim.\n\nThe cylinders were seized and produced before the Kandy Magistrate\u2019s Court as case productions.\n\nFollowing the proceedings, the Court imposed a fine on the trader and ordered that all 28 cylinders be confiscated and forfeited to the State.\n\nUnder Section 16(a) of the Consumer Affairs Authority Act No. 9 of 2003, traders are prohibited from falsely claiming that goods are unavailable when they have such goods in their possession for sale.\n\nThe CAA said it would continue raids and investigations to prevent traders from concealing goods and misleading consumers.\n\nConsumers who come across similar practices can inform the CAA by calling its 1977 hotline during office hours."
  },
