    "md5": "9403cb07436e89623b7b0e98627a9564",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1919,
    "chunk_text": "Moscow has repeatedly denied involvement in sabotage or hybrid warfare operations. Reuters could not establish who was \u200bbehind Monday's attacks or whether they were linked to the incidents in France.\n\n\"All IT systems are potentially vulnerable, and AI can now be used to successfully exploit these weaknesses \u2014 especially by sophisticated actors,\" she said.\n\nFrom refrigerators and heating systems to security cameras and alarms, an expanding range of devices once largely mechanical can now be monitored and controlled remotely, creating new opportunities for cybercriminals.\n\nAt least some of the refrigerator units affected on Monday used temperature control technology from Danish firm Danfoss that was also targeted in the French \u200battack. The firm said it had been working with customers to implement fixes.\n\nThe European Commission said the latest incidents highlighted how digital threats are becoming increasingly disruptive.\n\n\"They are a deliberate attempt to disrupt our food supply chain and undermine \u200bconsumers' confidence in it \u2013 a warning that we must take seriously,\" said EU commissioner for agriculture Christophe Hansen. \"The repeated occurrence of these cyberattacks is deeply concerning.\"\n\nA spokesperson for Colruyt Group, which operates Spar stores in Belgium under a franchise system, said five shops \u200chad their \u2060fridge systems attacked.\n\nIn Ireland, wholesaler Musgrave said the incident affected systems in 13 of its SuperValu stores, forcing it to remove some chilled and frozen products from sale.\n\n\"Our monitoring systems alerted us to the issue and we took immediate action,\" it said in a statement. \"Our investigation is ongoing.\"\n\nTom Hegel, a researcher at cybersecurity firm SentinelOne, said such attacks were typically linked to extortion, political motives or nation-state operations, with the absence of financial demands in recent cases pointing instead to sabotage."
