    "chunk_text": "This is an illustration of design, not a finished proposal. The final width and rates are for policymakers, who must weigh the revenue effect and the available fiscal space. The principles, however, are clear:\n\n2. Keep the burden balanced between individuals and corporates, as it broadly is today, so that salaried earners do not become the default source of new revenue.\n\n3. Deliver relief by reshaping the slabs, so that it reaches the middle and keeps taxpayers within the net.\n\n4. Publish the revenue cost and the distribution of benefits alongside the Budget, so that the public can judge the fairness of the system as well as its yield.\n\nTax relief that reaches the common man should leave him better off and keep the system strong enough to serve him. A revised individual tax slab structure, alongside a wider base, can do both.\n\n(The views and opinions expressed in this article are those of the author in her personal capacity. Reference has been made to the Inland Revenue Department\u2019s Annual Performance Report 2025)"
