    "chunk_size_bytes": 2004,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Connect 2026 positions Sri Lanka as a strategic partner for Indonesian investment\n\nSri Lanka\u2013Indonesia Business and Investment Forum in Jakarta brings policymakers, investment promotion agencies and business leaders together under the theme \u201cBridging Markets, Unlocking Growth\u201d\n\nThe Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) participated in Sri Lanka Connect 2026, the Sri Lanka\u2013Indonesia Business and Investment Forum organised by the Embassy of Sri Lanka in Jakarta on 16 October 2026 at the JW Marriott Hotel, Jakarta.\n\nConvened under the theme \u201cBridging Markets, Unlocking Growth\u201d, the forum was designed to strengthen economic cooperation between the two nations by fostering two-way investment, commercial and strategic partnerships, and policy dialogue. It offered policymakers, investment promotion agencies, business leaders, and investors from both countries a platform to exchange perspectives, showcase investment opportunities, and identify new avenues for collaboration.\n\nThe forum featured a keynote address by Indonesia\u203as Minister of Investment and Downstream Industry Rosan Roeslani and a video message from Sri Lanka\u203as Deputy Minister of Economic Development Nishantha Jayaweera.\n\nSri Lanka: the best business destination in Asia to grow your business\n\nThe opening panel presented Sri Lanka as a strategic investment destination in South Asia, highlighting its access to regional markets, advantageous geographical location and business-friendly investment environment.\n\nPanelists at Connect 2026 Jakarta examined why Sri Lanka is an ideal destination for foreign direct investment, including government incentives and policy support, ease of doing business, opportunities within landmark national development projects, and Public-Private Partnership opportunities. Priority sectors showcased included: Real Estate Development; Logistics and Supply Chain; Maritime and Port-related Industries; Textile and Apparel and Pharmaceuticals and Healthcare Manufacturing."
