    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka strengthens UK business ties ahead of Expo 2027\n\nBusiness and Investment Forum highlights economic recovery and investment opportunities\n\nInvites UK businesses, investors to participate at Sri Lanka Expo 2027 in Jan.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), in collaboration with the Sri Lanka High Commission in the United Kingdom, conducted a two-day business outreach program in London on 21 and 22 October 2026 to promote Sri Lanka Expo 2027 and encourage greater participation by UK businesses.\n\nThe move featured a Business and Investment Forum and networking session on 21 October, followed by bilateral business meetings on 22 October. Around 140 participants, including British buyers, investors, representatives of chambers of commerce, business associations and trade promotion organisations, attended the forum to explore commercial partnerships and strengthen trade and investment ties between the two countries.\n\nThe initiative aimed to expand market opportunities for Sri Lankan exports, promote the country as a reliable sourcing destination and showcase investment prospects across key sectors. Sri Lanka Expo 2027 is scheduled to take place from 14-17 January 2027.\n\nThe Sri Lankan delegation was led by Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe. Other members included Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara, EDB Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe, and the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) Executive Director.\n\nAddressing the forum, Minister Samarasinghe highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery, noting that the economy recorded growth of 5% in both 2024 and 2025."
