    "chunk_size_bytes": 1983,
    "chunk_text": "Who are the victims of the deadly Florida jet crash?\n\nBBC - Nine people have been killed after a small jet crashed and exploded in Florida on Sunday. The Learjet 60 was bound for the Bahamas from Austin when it nosedived into a multi-lane highway.\n\nThe National Transportation Safety Board is investigating whether ice and turbulence contributed to the crash, and whether human error played a role.\n\nThe Texas tech entrepreneur, his wife Helen Sharp and their two children, Emma, 4, and Charlie, 2, were all killed in the crash, according to a joint statement from some of the families of those killed.\n\nTheir family described them as \"devoted parents\" and said their children were \"the light of their lives\".\n\n\"Helen and Adam were the love affair that will last forever. Their warmth, generosity and gift for making people feel welcome touched so many lives,\" the statement reads.\n\nOn his LinkedIn page, Robinson described himself as the founder and CEO of RB2B and Retention.com, and the CEO of Moltsets.\n\nHe previously worked at global financial services business Lehman Brothers and the banking group Barclays.\n\nFellow tech entrepreneur Jesse Ouellette posted on LinkedIn about Robinson's death, saying he had helped him when he was building his company.\n\n\"He became a friend and someone I saw eye to eye with on how to build software companies,\" wrote Ouellette.\n\n\"He could disagree with you about almost anything, and somehow you'd walk away liking him even more.\"\n\nRobinson's last post on the networking site was on Sunday, about a debate he and Ouellette had scheduled for the following week.\n\nHelen Sharp, meanwhile, was an artist, according to media reports.\n\nHer father, Dudley Sharp, told the Florida news site The Palm Beach Post that news his family had been on the plane was \"quite a blow\".\n\n\"We had a daughter, her husband and two grandchildren on the plane,\" he said.\n\nReed, Fehr and Cetina were also travelling aboard the jet with Robinson Sharp and their children."
