    "language": "en",
    "md5": "4ff42c9c4791b5f2e159ecf06d6e2ad0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "DIMO Healthcare installs SL\u2019s first Deep Resolve AI-equipped MRI Scanner\n\nDIMO Healthcare has successfully completed the installation of the Siemens Healthineers MAGNETOM Sola 1.5T MRI system at Hemas Hospital Thalawathugoda, marking the installation of Sri Lanka\u2019s first MRI system equipped with Deep Resolve AI technology from Siemens Healthineers.\n\nThe installation is backed by DIMO Healthcare\u2019s dedicated service support, ensuring maximum operational efficiency.\n\nDeep Resolve is an AI-powered image reconstruction technology that uses deep learning to reduce noise and enhance image quality and resolution. It can reduce scan times by up to 73 percent and offer double the resolution of conventional scanning techniques.By supporting shorter scan times and reducing the potential for motion-related image degradation, Deep Resolve AI makes a significant improvement in the overall patient experience during an MRI scan.\n\nWijith Pushpawela, Executive Director of DIMO said, \u201cThe installation of the country\u2019s first MRI system with Deep Resolve technology marks a significant milestone in the expansion of Sri Lanka\u2019s diagnostic imaging capabilities. Our role extends beyond supplying technology. From installation and commissioning to application training and ongoing technical support, we work closely with healthcare providers to ensure advanced medical systems are effectively integrated into clinical practice.\u201d\n\nDr. Lakith Peiris, Managing Director of Hemas Hospitals & Laboratory Chain, said, \u201cAt Hemas Hospital Thalawathugoda, we continue to invest in technology that improves our capacity to deliver accurate and timely diagnostic care. This cutting-edge MRI system brings better care to our patients and provides ourhealthcare professionals withaccess to advanced diagnostic tools. We are excited about the value this technology will bring to patient care and are happy to have worked with DIMO Healthcare to implement it in our hospital.\u201d"
  },
