    "md5": "584f07c4a43dc533df4b3bea0cc4c8fe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1893,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys Mobility enters Sri Lanka\u2019s two-wheeler market\n\nThe unveiling of the all-new CFMOTO 450MT by Hayleys PLC Chairman and Chief Executive Mohan Pandithage and Executive Director Sarath Ganegoda. Hayleys Fentons Managing Director Hasith Prematillake looks on\n\nHayleys Mobility Limited, the mobility arm of Hayleys Fentons Limited, a Hayleys Group member, has entered Sri Lanka\u2019s two-wheeler market, introducing premium motorcycles from China\u2019s CFMOTO, one of the world\u2019s leading powersports and motorcycle brands and ZEEHO electric scooters.\n\nThe launch expands Hayleys Mobility\u2019s portfolio across adventure touring, sport riding, cruising and everyday commuting. CFMOTO\u2019s line-up is led by the 450MT adventure motorcycle and includes the 125NK and 250NK naked street bikes, the 250SR and 450SR sport motorcycles, and the 250CL-C cruiser. The 150AURA classic scooter and 150SC further extend the offering for riders seeking convenient options for everyday urban travel. Complementing this range, ZEEHO (the dedicated electric urban mobility sub-brand of CFMOTO) has introduced mobility options through its AE and EZ series, including the AE4, AE7 Pro and AE8 Max, alongside EZ3i and EZ4.\n\nSpeaking to Mirror Business, Hayleys Fentons Managing Director Hasith Prematillake said the entry into the two-wheeler market of Sri Lanka marks an important step in broadening the company\u2019s portfolio and reaching new customer segments. \u201cCFMOTO is not for the mass market. It\u2019s a bike for the niche market consisting Gen-Z and tech-savvy urban riders, focusing on connected, sustainable, and high-performance city commuting. It\u2019s not a market that existed in Sri Lanka. What was available here was a market for used, reconditioned Japanese bikes in the 300cc - 450cc range. With our entry, we have created a market for brand new CFMOTO bikes, and we don\u2019t see any competition.\u201d"
  },
