    "chunk_text": "Nadika said, \u201cI am honoured to assume the leadership of CFA Society Sri Lanka, an institution that has played a pivotal role in shaping my professional journey. As the financial services industry continues to evolve, the society\u2019s mission of promoting ethical conduct, professional excellence and lifelong learning remains more important than ever. I look forward to working closely with our members, volunteers and stakeholders to further strengthen the investment profession and contribute to the continued development of Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets.\u201d\n\nPrior to joining NDB, she served as Chief Executive Officer Investment Banking and Head of Credit at Asia Securities Advisors (Pvt.) Ltd. She has also held senior leadership positions as Head of Corporate Ratings at Fitch Ratings Lanka and Head of Fixed Income Research at Acuity Knowledge Partners, Sri Lanka.\n\nHer diverse professional experience across banking, investment research, credit ratings and corporate strategy brings valuable perspectives to her new role as President.\n\nNadika also holds a Bachelor of Laws (Honours) from the Faculty of Law, University of Colombo\n\nNadika assumes the presidency following a significant milestone in the society\u2019s history, as CFA Society Sri Lanka celebrated its 25th anniversary in 2026. Over the past two and a half decades, the society has played an important role in promoting ethical standards, professional development and investment excellence in Sri Lanka. Her appointment marks a new chapter in building on this legacy, strengthening engagement with the members and stakeholders and further advancing the society\u2019s contribution to the development of Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets.\n\nCFA Society Sri Lanka warmly congratulates Nadika on her appointment and looks forward to her leadership in further advancing the society\u2019s mission and strategic priorities."
