    "md5": "11c06a38264cccdad6ade5929908d79c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1941,
    "chunk_text": "Sunshine September-quarter profit rises 82.4% to Rs.2.3bn\n\nSunshine Holdings PLC\u2019s consolidated profit after tax rose 82.4 percent year-on-year to Rs.2.3 billion in the quarter ended September 30, 2026, as the revenue growth accelerated, although its six-month results showed continued pressure on the operating margins.\n\nThe group revenue increased 32 percent to Rs.21.6 billion in the second quarter of the financial year ending March 2027. The healthcare revenue grew 20.5 percent, while the tea export revenue rose 60.9 percent, supported by additional business from key customers and a higher contribution from the value-added products.\n\nThe stronger quarter lifted the consolidated profit after tax for the six months ended September to Rs.3.7 billion, up 44.3 percent from a year earlier. The first-half revenue increased 24.4 percent to Rs.40.2 billion. However, the profit growth outpaced the improvement in the operating earnings. The higher net finance income and a lower effective tax rate supported the six-month bottom line, while the earnings before interest and taxes rose 10.5 percent to Rs.6.1 billion.\n\nThe group\u2019s operating profit margin narrowed to 15.1 percent, from 17 percent. Gross profit increased 11.7 percent to Rs.11.5 billion but the gross margin fell to 28.7 percent, from 31.9 percent, reflecting the regulated pharmaceutical price reductions and the impact of a weaker rupee on the healthcare operations. The net profit margin nevertheless improved to 9.2 percent, from 8 percent.\n\nHealthcare remained the largest revenue contributor, accounting for 49 percent of the first-half turnover, followed by consumer operations at 37 percent and agribusiness at 14 percent.\n\nThe healthcare revenue increased 13.3 percent to Rs.19.6 billion over the six months, although its operating margin declined to 11.2 percent, from 13.1 percent as the pricing restrictions and higher import costs weighed on the earnings."
  },
