    "chunk_size_bytes": 1980,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka strengthens UK business ties ahead of Expo 2027\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), in collaboration with the Sri Lanka High Commission in the United Kingdom, conducted a two-day business outreach programme in London on October 21 and 22, 2026, to promote Sri Lanka Expo 2027 and encourage greater participation by the UK businesses.\n\nThe programme featured a Business and Investment Forum and networking session on October 21, followed by bilateral business meetings on October 22. Approximately 140 participants, including British buyers, investors, representatives of chambers of commerce, business associations and trade promotion organisations, attended the forum to explore commercial partnerships and strengthen trade and investment ties between the two countries.\n\nThe initiative aimed to expand market opportunities for Sri Lankan exports, promote the country as a reliable sourcing destination and showcase investment prospects across key sectors. Sri Lanka Expo 2027 is scheduled to take place from January 14 to 17, 2027.\n\nThe Sri Lankan delegation was led by Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe. The other members included Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara, EDB Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe and the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) Executive Director.\n\nAddressing the forum, Samarasinghe highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery, noting that the economy recorded growth of 5 percent in both 2024 and 2025.\n\nHe attributed the progress to the resilience of the Sri Lankan people, determination of the business community and advances made under the country\u2019s economic reform programme.\n\nHe also emphasised the government\u2019s continued efforts to improve the regulatory environment, streamline procedures, strengthen institutional coordination and enhance transparency and efficiency in public service delivery."
  },
