    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "He also emphasised the government\u2019s continued efforts to improve the regulatory environment, streamline procedures, strengthen institutional coordination and enhance transparency and efficiency in public service delivery.\n\nShe also highlighted the improvements in the country\u2019s fiscal position, including a budget deficit equivalent to 2.3 percent of gross domestic product and a declining debt ratio.\n\nShe further stated that foreign direct investment exceeded US $ 1 billion in 2025, representing an increase of 72 percent. These developments, she noted, demonstrated the opportunities available to investors seeking to establish or expand their presence in Sri Lanka.\n\nDelivering the welcome address, High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to the United Kingdom Nimal Senadheera highlighted the long-standing trade relationship between the two countries.\n\nHe also drew attention to the opportunities available to Sri Lankan exporters under the United Kingdom\u2019s Developing Countries Trading Scheme, which provides preferential market access for the eligible exports.\n\nWijesinghe outlined Sri Lanka\u2019s export potential in the UK market, highlighting the strengths of the country\u2019s products and services across key sectors. He emphasised Sri Lanka\u2019s competitiveness as a sourcing destination, supported by sustainable manufacturing practices, authentic products and compliance with international quality standards.\n\nHe also delivered a detailed presentation on Sri Lanka Expo 2027, describing the event as an important platform for international buyers and investors to engage directly with Sri Lankan businesses across a wide range of sectors.\n\nHe invited the UK-based companies to participate in the expo and explore sourcing, investment and partnership opportunities with Sri Lankan enterprises committed to international quality and sustainability standards."
