    "chunk_text": "EPF raises ACL Cables stake to 10%\n\nThe Employees\u2019 Provident Fund (EPF) increased its stake in ACL Cables PLC to 10 percent by end-September, adding just over three million shares during the quarter, according to a stock exchange disclosure.\n\nThe EPF held 71.87 million shares as at September 30, 2026, up from 68.86 million shares or 9.6 percent at end-June.\n\nThe increase amounted to 3,013,582 shares, lifting its ownership by 0.4 percentage points over the three months.\n\nIn an October 30 filing to the Colombo Stock Exchange, company secretary Corporate Affairs (Private) Limited said the EPF\u2019s holding had reached 10 percent of ACL Cables\u2019 issued share capital through a series of transactions.\n\nThe disclosure was made pursuant to Appendix 8A of the exchange\u2019s Listing Rules. It did not disclose the purchase prices or total value of the transactions."
