    "chunk_size_bytes": 929,
    "chunk_text": "Right now, I am writing a novel titled Kuzhandhai Veeran (Child Hero). It is the story of a young boy who was severely affected by the war. Additionally, my short story collection titled Yaazh Sumandha Siruvan (The Boy Who Carried the Yaazh) is scheduled to be released at the end of this year. This collection also mostly features stories about women and children affected by the war.\n\nToday, even a Tamil writer who writes a book for school children is under intense surveillance by military intelligence. Shadow book bans and the surveillance of writers are the major factors damaging Tamil literature today.\n\nTherefore, I would like to make a request to the Government and the authorities. Please allow us to remember our memories. Please allow us to tell our stories. Please allow the Sinhala readers to read our stories. They are certainly the stories that Sinhala people in the south and the global community need to know."
