    "md5": "cf96536bb809434fe0494933c0a08d33",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1331,
    "chunk_text": "Cyclone Murasu makes landfall on India\u2019s eastern coast\n\nReuters\u00a0- Cyclone Murasu made landfall \u200balong India's eastern coast on Tuesday, the country's \u200cweather department said, the second storm to hit the region in a week as authorities evacuated thousands of people to safety.\n\nThe \u200bIndia Meteorological Department said the severe cyclonic storm \u200bcrossed the coast of the south-eastern state of \u2060Andhra Pradesh between 03:30 and 05:30 local time, with \u200bwind speeds of 100-110 kph (62 to 68 mph) and gusts \u200bof up to 120 kph.\n\nNo deaths or injuries have been reported so far, although some trees and electric poles were uprooted, \u200bPrakhar Jain, Managing Director of the Andhra Pradesh State \u200bDisaster Management Authority, said.\n\nAuthorities began evacuating thousands of people on Monday \u200cand \u2060planned to move some 30,000 to safety in Andhra Pradesh, which is in the path of the cyclone.\n\nCyclone Murasu formed over the Bay of Bengal, a major region for \u200btropical cyclones \u200bthat has \u2060spawned deadly storms on India's east coast.\n\nIMD forecasts said the states of Andhra Pradesh and \u200bTamil Nadu to its south would be \u200bworst \u2060hit.\n\nAt least six people were killed in Cyclone Arnab, which was classified by IMD as a very severe cyclonic storm and \u2060made \u200blandfall in Andhra Pradesh on Wednesday."
  },
