    "chunk_size_bytes": 717,
    "chunk_text": "Krrish case: Namal released on bail\n\nColombo, Nov. 3 (Daily Mirror) - Parliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa and former Krrish\u00a0Company Director Janaki Siriwardena, who were arrested by the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) over an alleged Rs. 70 million bribe, were ordered to be released on bail by Colombo Chief Magistrate Asanga S. Bodaragama.\n\nThe Magistrate ordered each suspect to be released on three surety bails of Rs. 5 million each and a cash bail of Rs. 100,000.\n\nThe Magistrate also imposed a travel ban on both suspects and ordered them not to interfere with or exert any influence on prosecution witnesses.\n\nKrrish deal case: Namal Rajapaksa\u2019s bail order on November 3"
