    "md5": "029c98da4bd42ef74360f2843d66425b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1633,
    "chunk_text": "Culinary skills vital to strengthening tourism industry: Herath\n\nColombo, Nov. 3 (Daily Mirror) - Investing in people and developing professional skills are essential to strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry and creating better employment opportunities for young people, Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath said.\n\nAddressing the awards ceremony of the Nestl\u00e9 Golden Chef\u2019s Hat Competition 2026 at Cinnamon Life \u2013 City of Dreams, Colombo, on November 1, the Minister said Sri Lanka\u2019s culinary traditions could play an important role in attracting international tourists.\n\nHe said the country should promote its distinctive cuisine, local ingredients and cultural heritage internationally while preserving their authenticity and maintaining international standards.\n\nThe Minister highlighted the need to develop culinary and hospitality skills among young people and strengthen cooperation between the private sector, professional associations and educational institutions to produce skilled professionals for the industry.\n\nHe also said providing young people with opportunities to showcase their talents was important in developing future careers in the hospitality sector.\n\nCommending the participation of more than 1,500 students in the Junior Nestl\u00e9 Golden Chef\u2019s Hat Competition, Herath said such initiatives helped nurture young talent and create opportunities in the tourism and hospitality industries.\n\nHe congratulated the winners, finalists and participants and appreciated Nestl\u00e9 Lanka and its partners for their contribution to developing culinary talent in Sri Lanka."
  },
