    "chunk_text": "Explosions hit Iran\u2019s Qeshm Island as US media report US strikes in Hormuz\n\nALJAZEERA - Several explosions have been heard on Iran\u2019s Qeshm Island, as media outlets in the United States reported that the US military carried out what officials called \u201cdefensive strikes\u201d in the Strait of Hormuz.\n\nThe blasts came in rapid succession late on Monday, according to Iran\u2019s state-owned IRNA news agency. Witnesses told the agency they saw two planes flying over the island, located off Iran\u2019s southern coast near the Strait of Hormuz.\n\nThe semi-official Fars news agency said explosions were also heard in the port city of Bandar Lengeh, coming from the direction of the sea.\n\nThe Wall Street Journal, citing US officials, reported that the US military carried out the strikes.\n\nSome officials told the Journal the strikes were defensive, aimed at restricting Iran\u2019s ability to attack commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz. One official said Washington had deliberately kept the campaign quiet to avoid signalling a return to major combat operations.\n\nThe Associated Press news agency also cited a US official as saying the US had conducted defensive strikes against Iranian targets in the Strait of Hormuz. The official said that \u201cIranians using surface-to-air missiles against US assets\u201d had been targeted.\n\nReporters with Fox News and Axios said the attacks were in response to Iran\u2019s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) firing at a US aircraft in the Strait of Hormuz on Monday. Citing a US official, Fox News reporter Jennifer Griffin said the incident did not mark \u201cthe start of expanded strikes by the US\u201d.\n\nThere was no immediate comment from authorities in Iran or the US.\n\nOil prices rose more than $1 early on Tuesday amid concerns of risks to energy supplies.\n\nUS West Texas Intermediate crude was up $1.60, at $98.06 \u2060a barrel while Brent crude futures rose $1.84 to $106.61 a barrel by 07:44 GMT."
