    "md5": "d4963cfcaec0b82424ab39c66168d293",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1757,
    "chunk_text": "LAUGFS Gas expects three LPG shipments in November\n\nColombo, Nov. 3 (Daily Mirror) - LAUGFS Gas PLC has arranged three LPG shipments expected to arrive in Sri Lanka during November as the company seeks regulatory approval to resume domestic supplies through its Hambantota terminal.\n\nAccording to the company, the first shipment from OQT is expected to arrive at Hambantota Port between November 12 and 14, while a Geogas shipment is scheduled to arrive at Colombo Port between November 15 and 17. A third shipment from OQT is expected at Hambantota between November 24 and 28. However, the arrival dates remain subject to shipping arrangements, port operations and regulatory approvals.\n\nThe company said distribution was expected to resume gradually following the arrival and clearance of the cargoes, subject to the necessary authorisations for domestic releases from the Hambantota terminal.\n\nIn a statement, LAUGFS Gas apologised for the difficulties caused to households and businesses by the ongoing supply disruptions and said it remained committed to restoring LPG availability.\n\nThe company attributed the supply challenges partly to the conflict in the Middle East and disruptions to maritime transport through the Strait of Hormuz, which have affected international LPG supply chains and created procurement and shipping difficulties for Sri Lanka and other importing countries.\n\nMeanwhile, LAUGFS Terminals Ltd., a wholly owned subsidiary of LAUGFS Gas, has sought three months of temporary permission to use its Hambantota terminal for domestic LPG supplies. The US$65 million facility, which commenced operations in 2019, has a storage capacity of 30,000 metric tonnes and is Sri Lanka's largest LPG receiving, storage and entrep\u00f4t terminal."
  },
